      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ahh ok, thanks for the background. In addition to host drivers requirement to use `pkvm_memcache`, the other reason was - hypercall params `pkvm_domain_param` and `pkvm_iommu_map_param` also includes `pkvm_memcache`. Since kvm_host.h includes pkvm.h, I thought it would be better to move to pkvm.h so that kvm_host.h gets these from pkvm.h and the hypercall params can include `pkvm_memcache` seamlessly. \n\nIn 6.18, since kvm_pkvm.h includes kvm_host.h, it should be straightforward and we will not have any issues - kvm_host.h will have `pkvm_memcache` and kvm_pkvm.h can have the hypercall params.\n\nIs it okay to keep this patch as it is and add more context in the commit message as to why we are doing this?",
